<section class="section section--paper" id="types" aria-labelledby="s2-title">
  <div class="container">
    <header class="shead">
      <div class="shead__meta"></div>
      <div class="shead__body">
        <h2 class="shead__title rv" id="s2-title">Our LLM Security Testing Services</h2>
        <p class="shead__lede rv" style="--d:1">Each engagement is scoped to your application and combines manual attack techniques with automated coverage. These are the areas we test, from the first prompt to the systems the model can reach.</p>
      </div>
    </header>

    <div class="ledger">
      <article class="ledger__cell rv">
        <div class="ledger__head">{{ icon("syringe") }}</div>
        <h3 class="ledger__title">Prompt Injection Testing</h3>
        <p class="ledger__text">We test direct and indirect prompt injection, including instructions hidden in documents, web pages and emails the model reads. The goal is to show whether untrusted text can change what the application does.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="ledger__cell rv" style="--d:1">
        <div class="ledger__head">{{ icon("shield-crack") }}</div>
        <h3 class="ledger__title">Jailbreak and Guardrail Bypass Testing</h3>
        <p class="ledger__text">Our testers try role-play, encoding, multi-turn and obfuscation techniques against your content filters and safety instructions. Findings show which protections hold and which can be talked around.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="ledger__cell rv" style="--d:2">
        <div class="ledger__head">{{ icon("eye-off") }}</div>
        <h3 class="ledger__title">Sensitive Data and System Prompt Leakage Testing</h3>
        <p class="ledger__text">We check whether the model can be made to reveal its system prompt, credentials, personal data or another user's information, and whether sensitive details appear in responses, logs or error messages.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="ledger__cell rv" style="--d:3">
        <div class="ledger__head">{{ icon("terminal") }}</div>
        <h3 class="ledger__title">Insecure Output Handling Testing</h3>
        <p class="ledger__text">Model output is untrusted input to the rest of your application. We test whether responses can inject scripts, queries, links or commands into the pages, databases and systems that consume them.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="ledger__cell rv">
        <div class="ledger__head">{{ icon("api") }}</div>
        <h3 class="ledger__title">LLM Tool, Plugin and Function-Calling Testing</h3>
        <p class="ledger__text">When a model can call tools or APIs, we test what it is allowed to do, whether each action is authorized outside the prompt, and whether an attacker can steer the model into actions the user never intended.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="ledger__cell rv" style="--d:1">
        <div class="ledger__head">{{ icon("database") }}</div>
        <h3 class="ledger__title">RAG and Vector Store Security Testing</h3>
        <p class="ledger__text">For retrieval-augmented applications we test whether retrieval respects user permissions, whether poisoned documents can influence answers, and whether embeddings and knowledge bases expose more than they should.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="ledger__cell rv" style="--d:2">
        <div class="ledger__head">{{ icon("gauge") }}</div>
        <h3 class="ledger__title">LLM Abuse and Cost Controls Testing</h3>
        <p class="ledger__text">We examine rate limits, token budgets and request size controls to see whether an attacker can run up usage costs, exhaust capacity or degrade the service for legitimate users.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="ledger__cell rv" style="--d:3">
        <div class="ledger__head">{{ icon("dependency") }}</div>
        <h3 class="ledger__title">LLM Supply Chain and Configuration Review</h3>
        <p class="ledger__text">We review the models, libraries, plugins and third-party services your application depends on, along with API key handling and deployment settings, to find risks that sit outside your own code.</p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

