<!-- OWASP TOP 10 FOR LLM APPLICATIONS                                    -->
<!-- ================================================================== -->
<section class="section section--white" id="owasp" aria-labelledby="s3-title">
  <div class="container">
    <header class="shead">
      <div class="shead__meta"></div>
      <div class="shead__body">
        <h2 class="shead__title rv" id="s3-title">OWASP Top 10 for LLM Applications: What We Test</h2>
        <p class="shead__lede rv" style="--d:1">The OWASP Top 10 for LLM Applications is the most widely used reference for LLM risk. Our test coverage and reporting can follow it, so your findings are easy to share with engineering, security and compliance teams.</p>
      </div>
    </header>

    <div class="ledger ledger--10">
      <article class="ledger__cell rv">
        <div class="ledger__head">{{ icon("syringe") }}</div>
        <h3 class="ledger__title">Prompt Injection</h3>
        <p class="ledger__text">Crafted input that changes the model's behavior, whether typed by a user or hidden in content the model processes.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="ledger__cell rv" style="--d:1">
        <div class="ledger__head">{{ icon("unlock") }}</div>
        <h3 class="ledger__title">Sensitive Information Disclosure</h3>
        <p class="ledger__text">Personal data, business secrets or credentials returned in responses to the wrong person.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="ledger__cell rv" style="--d:2">
        <div class="ledger__head">{{ icon("link") }}</div>
        <h3 class="ledger__title">Supply Chain</h3>
        <p class="ledger__text">Risky models, datasets, libraries and plugins that the application inherits from outside vendors.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="ledger__cell rv">
        <div class="ledger__head">{{ icon("bug") }}</div>
        <h3 class="ledger__title">Data and Model Poisoning</h3>
        <p class="ledger__text">Tampered training, fine-tuning or retrieval data that quietly changes what the model says or does.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="ledger__cell rv" style="--d:1">
        <div class="ledger__head">{{ icon("terminal") }}</div>
        <h3 class="ledger__title">Improper Output Handling</h3>
        <p class="ledger__text">Model output passed to browsers, databases or shells without validation, opening the door to injection attacks.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="ledger__cell rv" style="--d:2">
        <div class="ledger__head">{{ icon("escalate") }}</div>
        <h3 class="ledger__title">Excessive Agency</h3>
        <p class="ledger__text">Models given more tools, permissions or autonomy than the task needs, so one bad instruction does real damage.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="ledger__cell rv">
        <div class="ledger__head">{{ icon("key") }}</div>
        <h3 class="ledger__title">System Prompt Leakage</h3>
        <p class="ledger__text">Hidden instructions, rules or embedded secrets that can be extracted and then used to plan a better attack.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="ledger__cell rv" style="--d:1">
        <div class="ledger__head">{{ icon("layers") }}</div>
        <h3 class="ledger__title">Vector and Embedding Weaknesses</h3>
        <p class="ledger__text">Retrieval stores that leak across users or can be manipulated to feed the model harmful content.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="ledger__cell rv" style="--d:2">
        <div class="ledger__head">{{ icon("alert") }}</div>
        <h3 class="ledger__title">Misinformation</h3>
        <p class="ledger__text">Confident but false output that people or systems act on, including invented facts, sources and code packages.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="ledger__cell rv">
        <div class="ledger__head">{{ icon("pulse") }}</div>
        <h3 class="ledger__title">Unbounded Consumption</h3>
        <p class="ledger__text">Requests that drive up compute cost, exhaust capacity or let an attacker copy the model's behavior at scale.</p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

