  <div class="container">
    <div class="process">
      <div class="process__aside">
        <h2 class="process__title" id="s5-title">Our LLM Security Testing Process</h2>
        <p class="process__lede">Every engagement follows the same structured path, from understanding how your application is built to confirming that each fix works. Automated payload libraries give broad coverage, and manual testing finds the issues automation misses.</p>
      </div>

      <ol class="process__list" data-process>
        <li class="step">
          <span class="step__marker" aria-hidden="true"></span>
          <h3 class="step__title">Scope, Architecture and Threat Modeling</h3>
          <p class="step__text">We start by mapping how the application works: the model, system prompt, data sources, tools and the users it serves. From that map we identify the attack paths that matter most and agree what is in scope.</p>
        </li>
        <li class="step">
          <span class="step__marker" aria-hidden="true"></span>
          <h3 class="step__title">Prompt Injection and Guardrail Testing</h3>
          <p class="step__text">Testers attempt direct and indirect prompt injection, jailbreaks and policy bypasses against the live application, combining payload libraries with hand-crafted, multi-turn attacks.</p>
        </li>
        <li class="step">
          <span class="step__marker" aria-hidden="true"></span>
          <h3 class="step__title">Data Exposure and Retrieval Testing</h3>
          <p class="step__text">We try to extract system prompts, personal data and documents the user should not see, and test whether retrieval honors access controls across accounts and roles.</p>
        </li>
        <li class="step">
          <span class="step__marker" aria-hidden="true"></span>
          <h3 class="step__title">Tool, Output and Integration Testing</h3>
          <p class="step__text">We test what the model can do through tools and APIs, whether those actions are authorized independently of the prompt, and how the application handles the output it receives back.</p>
        </li>
        <li class="step">
          <span class="step__marker" aria-hidden="true"></span>
          <h3 class="step__title">Risk Analysis and Reporting</h3>
          <p class="step__text">Each finding is validated, reproduced and rated by severity and business impact. The report explains the attack in plain terms and gives your developers a specific fix for each issue.</p>
        </li>
        <li class="step">
          <span class="step__marker" aria-hidden="true"></span>
          <h3 class="step__title">Remediation Support and Retesting</h3>
          <p class="step__text">We walk your team through the findings and answer questions as fixes are built. After remediation we retest to confirm that each issue is closed and that the changes have not opened new ones.</p>
        </li>
      </ol>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

