      <div class="shead__meta"></div>
      <div class="shead__body">
        <h2 class="shead__title rv" id="s6-title">What You Receive From Our LLM Security Testing</h2>
        <p class="shead__lede rv" style="--d:1">You receive a report your engineers can act on and your leadership can read. Every finding comes with the steps to reproduce it, the evidence, and a recommended fix.</p>
      </div>
    </header>

    <div class="deliver">
      <div class="deliver__media rv">
        <article class="xfind" aria-label="Example LLM security finding">
          <header class="xfind__head">
            <span class="xfind__tag">Example finding</span>
            <span class="xfind__sev">High</span>
          </header>
          <h3 class="xfind__title">Hidden instruction in an uploaded document makes the support assistant reveal another customer's order details</h3>
          <dl class="xfind__rows">
            <div><dt>Category</dt><dd>Indirect prompt injection · Sensitive information disclosure</dd></div>
            <div><dt>Evidence</dt><dd>A PDF containing hidden text told the assistant to look up and quote orders for a different account. The assistant called its order-lookup tool without checking who was signed in.</dd></div>
            <div><dt>Recommended fix</dt><dd>Authorize the lookup inside the order tool, not in the prompt. Treat uploaded text as untrusted data and filter responses for account identifiers.</dd></div>
            <div><dt>Retest</dt><dd>Fixed. The same attack no longer returns another account's data.</dd></div>
          </dl>
        </article>
      </div>
      <ol class="deliver__list">
        <li class="deliver__item rv">
          {{ icon("present") }}
          <div>
            <h3 class="deliver__title">Executive Summary</h3>
            <p class="deliver__text">A concise overview of the assessment that explains the main risks and their business impact, written for stakeholders who do not need the technical detail.</p>
          </div>
        </li>
        <li class="deliver__item rv">
          {{ icon("document") }}
          <div>
            <h3 class="deliver__title">Detailed LLM Vulnerability Report</h3>
            <p class="deliver__text">Every finding with its affected component, a description of the attack and its potential impact, mapped to the OWASP Top 10 for LLM Applications where relevant.</p>
          </div>
        </li>
        <li class="deliver__item rv">
          {{ icon("chart") }}
          <div>
            <h3 class="deliver__title">Severity and Risk Ratings</h3>
            <p class="deliver__text">Findings ranked by exploitability and business impact so your team knows what to fix first.</p>
          </div>
        </li>
        <li class="deliver__item rv">
          {{ icon("magnifier") }}
          <div>
            <h3 class="deliver__title">Reproducible Attack Evidence</h3>
            <p class="deliver__text">The exact prompts, inputs and responses behind each finding, so developers can reproduce the issue and verify their fix.</p>
          </div>
        </li>
        <li class="deliver__item rv">
          {{ icon("route") }}
